## Item 2 — hit-registry lifetime + route gating (auditA #2) — DONE (commit ae5524f)

Root cause: `set_transcript_hit_rows` (session.rs:304) and
`set_footer_location_hit` (session.rs:660) were written only by the
session render; `navigate()` (store.rs:3018, the only `route.set`)
never cleared them, and `mouse_event`'s Up(Left)/Moved arms read both
registries without a route gate — after Session → Home a release on a
stale row rect toggled the previous session's group / opened
WorkingDirectory with stale coords, and Moved could flip hover.

Fix: `Store::clear_route_pointer_registries()` on every navigate
(+ sidebar wheel geometry, item 1); Up(Left) transcript loop requires
`hit.session_id == route session`; footer-location Up + Moved hover
gated on `Route::Session`. Tests:
`route_change_clears_the_pointer_registries`,
`home_release_fires_no_stale_transcript_or_location_hits` (pins the
clear AND the gate independently via a re-injected stale row).

## Item 1 — mouse wheel everywhere (auditA #1) — DONE (commit e630880)

Root cause: `MouseEventKind::Scroll*` matched the catch-all `_ => {}`
arm — no wheel surface existed.

Fix (modal-first routing in `mouse_event`):
- dialog → `SelectState::scroll_window_by` (3 rows/notch, window
  only — the selection never moves, v2's dialog scrollbox);
- permission → consumed (the body renders all lines; no leak);
- sidebar columns → `Store::sidebar_scroll_by` (3/notch, clamped by
  `content_height - viewport`, geometry recorded by the session
  render; hidden pane/route change resets);
- transcript → one notch = `session.page.up/down` through the SAME
  `ScrollCommand::PageUp/PageDown` driver the keys use — the E1
  half-page math (±viewport/2, js_round half→+∞, sticky re-arm);
  `wheel_scrolls_the_transcript_half_a_page_per_notch` asserts the
  numeric landing AND equality with the `pageup` key path;
- diff-viewer hook point documented at the arm (dead code until it
  mounts — auditA §2.12).
Sidebar render: `render_sidebar_scrolled` (chrome pinned, slot
clipped at the footer stack); solid path threads the offset.

## Item 3 — permission pointer arms (auditA #4) — DONE (commit b98a8ce)

Root cause: the ask's pills/buttons render in
`footer/permission.rs` but `mouse_event`'s arms all early-returned
under `permission_live()` (app.rs:420) — v2 renders them as the
screen's only interactive surface (permission.tsx:375-400, 583-587).

Fix: `permission_pointer_hits()` (the pure layout twin of
`render_permission_controls`: pills from x=2 label+2-wide with 1-gap;
the reject stage's right-aligned `enter confirm`/`esc cancel` button
extents ending at width−4) + the store registry (recorded by
`App::frame`'s permission mount at absolute cells, controls row =
size.1−2; cleared on `permission_replied` and when no ask is live).
`mouse_event`: Moved over a pill selects; Up on a pill sets the
selection then runs the keyboard-enter path (reply through
`permission_replies` + local resolution); Up on the reject hint
buttons maps to the reject-stage enter/escape. The
transcript-protecting early return now sits INSIDE the permission
branch, after its own targets. Tests:
`permission_allow_once_via_pointer` (hover-select + reply + rect
teardown), `permission_reject_confirm_and_cancel_via_pointer` (the
full reject cycle + stray-release negative).

## Item 4 — all five disclosure surfaces (auditA #5) — DONE (commit f6ec08e)

Root cause: session.rs:313 armed only `group:Reasoning:` keys; the
`group:Exploration:`/`group:Activity:`/`group:Instructions:` rows
(message/list.rs:526's `row_key`) and the `thought:{mid}:{pid}` rows
(list.rs:216) rendered with the affordance but had no hit rows.

Fix: hit rows arm EVERY `group:` key (v2's `useDisclosure` toggle:
group-view.tsx:152/183/219/256 — plugin-rule kinds ride GroupContent
too) with the same glyph-tight rect; thought rows arm as
`ToggleThought` (the minimal-mode ReasoningHeader toggle,
message-parts.tsx:66-86) with the first line's glyphs. The render
honors a per-session collapsed set: a collapsed thought renders its
one-line `+ Thought: {title}` header (via `reasoning_header_row`)
instead of the bordered body — the port's stand-in for v2's
toggleable inline header (the always-grouping reducer never produces
the ungrouped form). Default renders unchanged — zero golden churn.
Expanded Exploration/Instructions CONTENT rides the missing tool-row
surface (auditA #9, out of lane): the state flip is v2-exact
(`setGroupExpanded`), the children render nothing yet either way.
Tests: `exploration_group_header_toggles`,
`thought_rows_toggle_their_disclosure`.

## Item 5 — the dialog close family (auditA #6) — DONE (commit df0a7eb)

Root cause: the port's dialog chrome renders the header's muted
`esc`/`esc/enter` label (v2's ~22 per-dialog close affordances, e.g.
dialog-help.tsx:25, dialog-confirm.tsx:64) and the Help `ok` pill —
all dead (backdrop/escape only).

Fix: `dialog_chrome_button_hits()` in dialog_solid.rs — the close
label's rect per family (select/plugin-rows paddingRight 4,
prompt/help paddingRight 2; Help's label is `esc/enter`) + the Help
ok pill (the button BOX: padding 3 + ok + padding 3, right-justified
on the last content row). v2's labels carry no hover styling — the
hit rect alone is the affordance. `render_overlay` records them with
the frame rect (cleared together); the Up(Left) dialog branch checks
the buttons FIRST (child-first bubbling): Close pops the dialog (the
port's per-dialog esc parity), HelpOk clears the stack
(dialog-help.tsx:39). Tests:
`dialog_header_close_label_releases_closed` (the rect hugs the
painted `esc` glyphs), `help_dialog_ok_button_and_esc_label_close`.
Note: the confirm-OK/export/error-details button rows belong to
dialogs the port does not have ((c) missing surfaces, auditA §2.7) —
out of this item's ✕-family scope.

## Bonus fix — the footer-location hit rect was one row high

The PTY proof clicked the PAINTED label and nothing opened: the rect
said `height−2` (session.rs:714) but the opentui-solid bridge paints
the prompt mount's footer row — the label — at `height−1`. Rect
fixed to the painted row (pre-existing since M3; no prior test
pinned the screen row — the unit tests inject the rect).

